<!-- 5. How the Process Works -->
<section class="sec" id="process">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div style="text-align:center;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
      <h2>What to Expect Working With Us</h2>
      <p class="lede">You don't need to have your paperwork figured out, and you don't need to know whether you qualify. We want to talk it through with you either way. Here's what happens after you reach out.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps" style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n"></div>
        <div class="stack-sm">
          <h3>1. Discovery Consultation</h3>
          <p>A relaxed call with someone who does this every day. We'll talk through a few simple questions, like who was affected, where they lived, and what their diagnosis was. Most people are surprised how much we can figure out from one conversation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n"></div>
        <div class="stack-sm">
          <h3>2. Immediate Honest Evaluation</h3>
          <p>We tell you right away where things stand. If your story qualifies for the Downwinders program, we say so and explain why. If not, we tell you that too, so you have clear answers either way.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n"></div>
        <div class="stack-sm">
          <h3>3. Getting Your Claim Ready</h3>
          <p>You'll have a dedicated account manager who walks you through exactly what's needed, step by step. Together you'll cover all the required documents, and for any you need help tracking down, we step in and handle it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n"></div>
        <div class="stack-sm">
          <h3>4. Claim Filing &amp; DOJ Tracking</h3>
          <p>Once your claim is ready, we review every document, then submit it on your behalf so it's done right the first time. From there, we handle all DOJ communication for you and know exactly who to reach if anything needs adjusting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

